LESSONS[19]={
  phase:'Phase 3 — Video Ads',
  title:'Day 19: AI Video Foundations — How It Actually Works',
  tools:['Kling 2.6','Google Flow','Runway Gen-4.5'],time:'55 min',tags:['video','foundations','prompting'],
  videos:[
    {title:'Kling 2.6 Complete Beginner to Pro Guide 2025',channel:'Theoretically Media',duration:'28:20',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+2.6+complete+guide+beginner+pro+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#0f0c29,#302b63)'},
    {title:'Runway Gen-4.5 Full Tutorial — Every Feature',channel:'Matt Wolfe',duration:'24:15',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=runway+gen+4.5+full+tutorial+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e,#16213e)'},
    {title:'AI Video vs Real Video — Can You Tell the Difference?',channel:'AI Advantage',duration:'16:40',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=AI+video+vs+real+video+kling+runway+2026+comparison',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#11998e,#38ef7d)'},
    {title:'The 4-Part Video Prompt Formula That Actually Works',channel:'Future Tech Pilot',duration:'19:30',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=AI+video+prompt+formula+kling+runway+professional+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#f7971e,#ffd200)'},
  ],
  inspiration:[
    {name:'Kling AI Official Showcase',desc:'Study the highest-rated community videos. Reverse-engineer the prompts from the results.',type:'website',url:'https://klingai.com/community',tag:'Reference'},
    {name:'Runway AI Explore Feed',desc:'See what professionals are creating with Runway Gen-4.5. Study camera movement and physics.',type:'website',url:'https://runwayml.com/explore',tag:'Inspiration'},
    {name:'Pinterest: AI Video Ads 2025',desc:'Search "AI generated video ad 2025" to see the current state of commercial AI video.',type:'pinterest',url:'https://pinterest.com/search/pins/?q=AI+generated+video+commercial+ad+2026',tag:'Mood Board'},
  ],
  imageRefs:[],
  content:'<div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon blue">🎬</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Why AI Video is Fundamentally Different from AI Images</div><div class="concept-card-sub">The mental model shift that changes everything</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Image generation is about <strong>describing a moment</strong>. Video generation is about describing a <strong>world with physics</strong>. Modern AI video models are world simulators — they calculate gravity, track objects through time, and maintain consistency across frames.</p><div class="highlight-box blue"><span class="hb-icon">🧠</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">The 4 Tool Mental Models (Memorize These)</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>Kling 2.6</strong> = Audio-visual choreographer. Describe what moves and generate audio + video together.<br><strong>Runway Gen-4.5</strong> = Kinetic sculptor. Describe forces and physics, not just visuals.<br><strong>Veo 3.1</strong> = Rendering engine. Structured, precise, ingredient-list descriptions.<br><strong>Sora 2</strong> = Physics simulator. Describe cause and effect, not just appearance.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon purple">📐</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">The Professional Video Prompt Formula</div><div class="concept-card-sub">Camera Movement + Subject + Motion + Context + Style + Physics + Endpoint</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Early AI video was a slot machine — type vague things, get random results. Professional video prompting has a clear formula that produces predictable, client-ready outputs.</p><div class="highlight-box amber"><span class="hb-icon">⚡</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">The 7-Layer Video Prompt Stack</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>1. Camera Movement</strong> (always first — most important layer)<br><strong>2. Shot Type</strong> (close-up, wide, overhead, POV)<br><strong>3. Subject + Action</strong> (who/what, doing what precisely)<br><strong>4. Environment + Lighting</strong> (setting, time, atmosphere)<br><strong>5. Physics Details</strong> (material behavior, weight, gravity)<br><strong>6. Style + Mood</strong> (cinematic language, brand aesthetic)<br><strong>7. Endpoint</strong> ("...then settles back into place" — prevents 99% hangs)</div></div></div><div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// PROFESSIONAL VIDEO PROMPT — KLING 2.6</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this,\'Slow orbital arc shot circling the product clockwise. Premium wireless headphones half-buried in golden desert sand, camera slowly orbits the product revealing dramatic sand dunes behind, warm golden hour light casting long shadows, subtle wind moves fine sand particles across surface, cinematic luxury brand aesthetic, hyperrealistic material rendering, 10 seconds, 16:9. Camera settles to front-facing position.\')">📋 Copy</button></div><div class="prompt-card-body"><span class="prompt-param">Slow orbital arc shot circling the product clockwise.</span> Premium wireless headphones half-buried in golden desert sand, camera slowly orbits the product revealing dramatic sand dunes behind, <span class="prompt-style">warm golden hour light casting long shadows</span>, subtle wind moves fine sand particles across surface, <span class="prompt-style">cinematic luxury brand aesthetic, hyperrealistic material rendering</span>, 10 seconds, 16:9. <span class="prompt-neg">Camera settles to front-facing position.</span></div></div></div></div><div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon amber">⚠️</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">The 5 Failures That Waste Your Credits</div><div class="concept-card-sub">Every professional learns these the hard way — you won\'t have to</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><ul class="steps-list"><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--red)">1</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Missing Camera Movement = Static Shot</div><div class="step-desc">No camera specification = Kling picks "static" by default. Always name the move first: push-in, orbit, tracking, dolly-out.</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--red)">2</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Open-Ended Motion = 99% Hang</div><div class="step-desc">If you write "hair moves in wind" — the AI doesn\'t know when to stop. Always add an endpoint: "...hair moves in wind, then settles back into place."</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--red)">3</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Too Many Elements = Chaos</div><div class="step-desc">Kling 2.6 handles 5-7 elements. More = distortion, object changes, impossible physics. Pick one hero action, hint at secondary motion only.</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--red)">4</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Redescribing Image in I2V Mode</div><div class="step-desc">Image-to-Video only needs motion instructions. The AI can already see the image. Describe what should MOVE, not what\'s already there.</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--red)">5</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Contradictory Instructions</div><div class="step-desc">"Slow motion fast-paced action" — contradictions confuse all models. Pick one speed, one direction, one physics state per generation.</div></div></li></ul></div></div> <div class="concept-card"> <div class="concept-card-head"> <div class="concept-icon green">🔧</div> <div> <div class="concept-card-title">Tool Spotlight: Google Flow + Kling 2.6</div> <div class="concept-card-sub">The two AI video platforms every designer needs in 2026</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card-body"> <p><strong>Google Flow</strong> (labs.google/fx/tools/flow) — AI filmmaking on Veo 3.1 with Nano Banana for image-to-video. Free daily credits. Cinematic clips, scene extension, camera control. <a href="https://labs.google/fx/tools/flow" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:700;">Open Flow →</a></p> <p><strong>Kling 2.6</strong> (kling.kuaishou.com) — Best dynamic motion and physics. 4K, 15s clips, native audio. Free tier. Superior for fabric, liquid, smoke. <a href="https://kling.kuaishou.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:700;">Open Kling →</a></p> <div class="highlight-box green"> <span class="hb-icon">⚖️</span> <div class="hb-content"> <div class="hb-title">Flow vs Kling</div> <div class="hb-text">Google Flow: scene composition, camera control, image-to-video. Kling: physics-heavy motion and text-to-video from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>',
  assignment:{title:'Day 19: First AI Video — Product in Motion',emoji:'🎬',desc:'Write and generate your first professional AI video using the 7-layer formula. Test both Text-to-Video and Image-to-Video. See the difference.',deliverables:['Product choice + campaign objective','Your 7-layer Text-to-Video prompt for Kling','Your Image-to-Video setup: which image did you animate and why?','What surprised you most about AI video generation?'],placeholder:'Product:\nObjective:\n\n7-layer TTV prompt:\n1. Subject:\n2. Motion:\n3. Camera:\n4. Environment:\n5. Lighting:\n6. Style:\n7. Technical:\n\nImage-to-Video: image description + what motion you added:\n\nBiggest surprise:',systemPrompt:'You are an AI video production director. Review the student\'s first video prompts. Is their 7-layer structure complete and specific? Are they confusing appearance language with motion language? Give specific feedback on the most common first-timer mistake in their submission. Max 230 words.'}
};

LESSONS[20]={
  phase:'Phase 3 — Video Ads',
  title:'Day 20: Camera Movement Mastery',
  tools:['Kling 2.6','Google Flow','Runway Gen-4.5'],time:'60 min',tags:['camera','cinematography','video'],
  videos:[
    {title:'Every Camera Movement Explained — Filmmaking 101',channel:'Film Riot',duration:'22:10',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=every+camera+movement+explained+filmmaking+cinematography+dolly+tracking',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a1a,#4a4a4a)'},
    {title:'AI Video Camera Control — Kling Orbital Shots',channel:'AI Advantage',duration:'18:30',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+ai+camera+movement+orbital+tracking+dolly+cinematic+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#0f0c29,#302b63)'},
    {title:'Runway Director Mode — Camera Control Deep Dive',channel:'Future Tech Pilot',duration:'20:15',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=runway+gen+4+director+mode+camera+control+tutorial+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e,#16213e)'},
  ],
  inspiration:[
    {name:'Shot Café — Cinematography Reference',desc:'Every shot type with visual examples. Use this to match camera movement names to what you want to achieve.',type:'website',url:'https://shotcafe.net',tag:'Reference'},
    {name:'Pinterest: Cinematic Camera Movement',desc:'Visual mood boards for each camera movement type — helps you visualize before prompting.',type:'pinterest',url:'https://pinterest.com/search/pins/?q=cinematic+camera+movement+film+reference',tag:'Visual Ref'},
  ],
  imageRefs:[],
  content:'<div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon purple">🎥</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Camera Movement is the Most Powerful Variable</div><div class="concept-card-sub">It changes meaning, emotion, and quality more than any other element</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>In traditional filmmaking, every camera movement is <strong>motivated</strong> — it serves a narrative or emotional purpose. Kling and Runway understand this language. Specifying motivated camera movement is the single fastest upgrade to your video quality.</p><div class="highlight-box blue"><span class="hb-icon">🎯</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">Motivated vs Decorative Camera Movement</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>Decorative (bad):</strong> "Camera pans across the scene" — no reason, no story<br><strong>Motivated (good):</strong> "Slow push-in as subject turns to face camera, building intimacy" — movement has purpose<br>Always ask: why is the camera moving? What does it reveal or feel?</div></div></div></div></div><div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon amber">🗂</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Complete Camera Movement Vocabulary</div><div class="concept-card-sub">Every move, its prompt term, and when to use it commercially</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><ul class="steps-list"><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">↗</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Push-In (Dolly In)</div><div class="step-desc">Camera physically moves toward subject. Use for: intimacy, tension, revealing expression, product detail. Prompt: "slow dolly push-in toward subject"</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">↙</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Pull-Out (Dolly Out)</div><div class="step-desc">Camera moves away. Use for: isolation, grand reveal, context reveal. Prompt: "slow pull-out dolly away from subject revealing the full environment"</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">⭕</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Orbital Arc / Orbit</div><div class="step-desc">Camera circles the subject. Best for product hero shots. Prompt: "smooth orbital arc shot circling product clockwise, maintaining product as central focal point"</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">→</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Tracking Shot</div><div class="step-desc">Camera follows subject laterally. Use for: walking shots, motion alongside subject. Prompt: "smooth lateral tracking shot following subject from the side"</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">↑</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Drone Ascent</div><div class="step-desc">Camera rises. Use for: scale reveals, epic establishing. Prompt: "drone ascending shot rising above subject, revealing vast landscape behind"</div></div></li><li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">⬇</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Crane/Tilt Down</div><div class="step-desc">Descend or tilt down. Use for: omniscient reveal, brand power. Prompt: "slow crane descent from aerial perspective down to subject level"</div></div></li></ul><div class="prompt-card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// RUNWAY: PRODUCT ORBIT + PHYSICS</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this,\'Low angle, smooth arc shot orbiting premium sneaker on wet dark asphalt clockwise. Camera: arc movement maintaining shoe as central focal point throughout. Lighting: neon reflections shift dynamically across surface as camera moves. Physics: shoe maintains perfect position and sharp focus throughout rotation. Commercial ad quality, 10 seconds 16:9.\')">📋 Copy</button></div><div class="prompt-card-body"><span class="prompt-param">Low angle, smooth arc shot orbiting premium sneaker on wet dark asphalt clockwise.</span> Camera: arc movement maintaining shoe as central focal point throughout. Lighting: neon reflections shift dynamically across surface as camera moves. <span class="prompt-style">Physics: shoe maintains perfect position and sharp focus throughout rotation.</span> Commercial ad quality, 10 seconds 16:9.</div></div></div></div> <div class="compare-section"> <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:10px;">🎬 Same Product — 2 Camera Languages</div> <div class="compare-toggle-bar"> <button class="compare-tab bad active" id="cmp20-a" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmp20\',\'bad\')">Push-In</button> <button class="compare-tab good" id="cmp20-b" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmp20\',\'good\')">Orbit/Arc</button> </div> <div class="compare-panel bad-panel active" id="cmp20-a-panel"> <div class="compare-prompt">Luxury watch. Camera: slow push-in from wide to tight close-up on the watch face over 8 seconds.</div> <div class="compare-annotation"><strong>Emotion: Reverence and desire.</strong> The slow approach builds anticipation. Used in luxury automotive, whisky campaigns, perfume reveals. The watch becomes worthy of attention. Use this when product detail IS the story.</div> </div> <div class="compare-panel good-panel" id="cmp20-b-panel"> <div class="compare-prompt">Luxury watch. Camera: smooth 270° orbit at mid-height, full rotation in 10 seconds.</div> <div class="compare-annotation"><strong>Emotion: Craftsmanship and completeness.</strong> The orbit shows every angle — case side, strap, clasp, crown. Used in product launch hero videos and e-commerce. Use this when product design is the selling point.</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card"> <div class="concept-card-head"> <div class="concept-icon amber">🎯</div> <div> <div class="concept-card-title">Camera Movement Decision Guide</div> <div class="concept-card-sub">Match the movement to the commercial purpose</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card-body"> <ul class="steps-list"> <li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">→</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Push-In</div><div class="step-desc">Building desire, revealing detail, creating tension. Best for: luxury goods, beauty closeups, product reveals. Prompt: "slow cinematic push-in, starting wide, ending in tight macro focus on..."</div></div></li> <li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">⟳</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Orbit / Arc</div><div class="step-desc">Showing all sides, demonstrating craftsmanship. Best for: product launches, watches, sneakers, tech devices. Prompt: "smooth 270° orbit at eye level, full rotation, product centered throughout..."</div></div></li> <li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">⇝</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Tracking / Follow</div><div class="step-desc">Energy, lifestyle, movement. Best for: fashion, fitness, food delivery. Prompt: "smooth tracking shot following subject laterally, keeps subject in frame center, handheld energy..."</div></div></li> <li class="step-item"><div class="step-num">↑</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Rising / Crane Up</div><div class="step-desc">Scale, aspiration, epic reveal. Best for: architecture, brand anthems. Prompt: "slow crane shot rising from ground level to aerial perspective, revealing cityscape behind..."</div></div></li> </ul> </div> </div>',
  assignment:{title:'Day 20: Camera Movement — 3 Tests',emoji:'🎥',desc:'Test 3 different camera movements with the same subject. Understand when each movement serves a different commercial purpose.',deliverables:['Product/subject chosen','Push-in prompt — with commercial purpose stated','Orbit/arc prompt — with commercial purpose stated','Tracking/dolly prompt — with commercial purpose stated'],placeholder:'Subject:\n\nPush-in prompt:\nCommercial purpose:\n\nOrbit/arc prompt:\nCommercial purpose:\n\nTracking prompt:\nCommercial purpose:\n\nWhich movement felt most cinematic — and for what type of brand:',systemPrompt:'You are a cinematographer and commercial video director. Review the student\'s 3 camera movement prompts. Are the movements specified with professional precision (slow push-in vs crash zoom)? Do the stated commercial purposes match the movement type? Correct any mismatches. Max 230 words.'}
};

LESSONS[21]={
  phase:'Phase 3 — Video Ads',
  title:'Day 21: Kling 2.6 Deep Mastery',
  tools:['Kling 2.6'],time:'65 min',tags:['kling','advanced','commercial'],
  videos:[
    {title:'Kling 2.6 Advanced Features — Everything New',channel:'Theoretically Media',duration:'26:40',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+2.6+advanced+features+everything+new+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#0f0c29,#302b63)'},
    {title:'Kling Elements Feature — Consistent Characters',channel:'AI Advantage',duration:'19:20',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+elements+feature+consistent+character+tutorial+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#667eea,#764ba2)'},
    {title:'Kling 2.6 Physics — Fabric, Liquid, Fire Mastery',channel:'Matt Wolfe',duration:'22:10',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+2.6+physics+fabric+liquid+fire+prompts+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#f7971e,#ffd200)'},
    {title:'Image to Video — Kling Professional Workflow',channel:'Future Tech Pilot',duration:'17:50',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=kling+image+to+video+professional+workflow+I2V+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#43e97b,#38f9d7)'},
  ],
  inspiration:[
    {name:'Kling Community — Top Rated Videos',desc:'Study the prompts behind the highest-rated videos. Most users share their prompts in comments.',type:'website',url:'https://klingai.com/community',tag:'Prompts'},
    {name:'Fal.ai Kling 2.6 Pro Guide',desc:'The most comprehensive prompt guide for Kling 2.6 Pro — bookmark this.',type:'website',url:'https://fal.ai/learn/devs/kling-2-6-pro-prompt-guide',tag:'Technical'},
    {name:'VEED: Kling AI Complete Guide',desc:'Full breakdown of every Kling model with specific prompt structures per model.',type:'website',url:'https://www.veed.io/learn/kling-ai-prompting-guide',tag:'Reference'},
  ],
  imageRefs:[],
  content:'<div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon blue">⚡</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Kling 2.6 — What Makes It Different</div><div class="concept-card-sub">Physics, audio, and the Elements feature change everything for commercial work</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Kling 2.6 is an <strong>audio-visual choreographer</strong>. Unlike other tools that only do video, Kling 2.6 natively generates synchronized audio — ambient sound, implied music, atmospheric effects — alongside the visual. For commercial ads, this is transformative.</p><div class="highlight-box blue"><span class="hb-icon">🎵</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">Kling 2.6 Unique Capabilities</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>Native audio generation:</strong> Describe ambient sound in your prompt ("soft wind, distant traffic hum")<br><strong>Physics simulation:</strong> Fabric, liquid, fire, smoke — all behave with genuine material physics<br><strong>Elements feature:</strong> Upload reference images to maintain character/product consistency across shots<br><strong>5-10s to 2 minutes:</strong> Longest output of any major model</div></div></div></div></div><div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon green">🧵</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Physics Prompting — Kling\'s Biggest Strength</div><div class="concept-card-sub">This is where Kling beats every other model</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Kling 2.6 understands material physics. But you need to <strong>describe behavior, not just appearance</strong>:</p><div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// FABRIC PHYSICS — CORRECT WAY</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this,\'Camera slowly pushes in on model standing in doorway. Silk evening gown fabric responds to gentle breeze from off-screen fan, fabric ripples with natural weight and flow physics, translucent areas catch the backlight, folds and creases behave realistically, then fabric settles into natural drape. Golden hour backlight, luxury fashion aesthetic, 10s 16:9.\')">📋 Copy</button></div><div class="prompt-card-body">Camera slowly pushes in on model standing in doorway. <span class="prompt-param">Silk evening gown fabric responds to gentle breeze from off-screen fan, fabric ripples with natural weight and flow physics, translucent areas catch the backlight, folds and creases behave realistically, then fabric settles into natural drape.</span> Golden hour backlight, luxury fashion aesthetic, 10s 16:9.</div></div><div class="prompt-card" style="margin-top:10px;"><div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// LIQUID PHYSICS — PRODUCT AD</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this,\'Static low angle macro shot. Premium whisky being poured into crystal glass, amber liquid cascades with realistic viscosity and surface tension, droplets scatter naturally, liquid catches single overhead rim light creating internal glow, bubbles rise and dissipate naturally. Dark wet slate surface, Johnnie Walker Blue aesthetic, 10s 16:9.\')">📋 Copy</button></div><div class="prompt-card-body">Static low angle macro shot. <span class="prompt-param">Premium whisky being poured into crystal glass, amber liquid cascades with realistic viscosity and surface tension, droplets scatter naturally, liquid catches single overhead rim light</span>, creating internal glow, bubbles rise and dissipate naturally. Dark wet slate surface, Johnnie Walker Blue aesthetic, 10s 16:9.</div></div></div></div><div class="compare-section"><div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:10px;">🎬 Beginner vs Expert — Same Shot</div><div class="compare-toggle-bar"><button class="compare-tab bad active" id="cmpd21-bad" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmpd21\',\'bad\')">❌ Beginner Prompt</button><button class="compare-tab good" id="cmpd21-good" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmpd21\',\'good\')">✅ Expert Prompt</button></div><div class="compare-panel bad-panel active" id="cmpd21-bad-panel"><div class="compare-prompt">"A woman walking on beach with dress flowing"</div><div class="compare-annotation"><strong>Problems:</strong> No camera movement, no physics description, no endpoint, vague subject, no style reference. Kling will generate a generic static shot.</div></div><div class="compare-panel good-panel" id="cmpd21-good-panel"><div class="compare-prompt">"Tracking shot following from the side. Tall 28-year-old woman in floor-length white linen dress walking slowly along shoreline at golden hour, fabric and hem respond to gentle sea breeze with natural linen drape and weight, wet sand reflects warm sunset light, gentle waves lap at edge of frame. Kinfolk lifestyle aesthetic, soft natural color grade, 10s 16:9. Dress fabric settles as she slows to a stop."</div><div class="compare-annotation"><strong>What changed:</strong> Named camera (tracking), specified fabric material (linen has different physics than silk), described the physics behavior with endpoint, specific lighting (golden hour + wet sand reflection), style reference, and proper endpoint to prevent 99% hang.</div></div></div>',
  assignment:{title:'Day 21: Kling Physics — 3 Material Tests',emoji:'🎬',desc:'Create 3 short Kling video prompts targeting 3 different physics behaviors: fabric flow, liquid pour, and atmospheric (smoke/steam). See which renders most realistically.',deliverables:['Fabric physics prompt — clothing, curtain, or material in motion','Liquid physics prompt — pour, splash, or flow','Atmospheric prompt — smoke, steam, mist, or fog','Which physics type rendered most convincingly — and why do you think Kling handles it better?'],placeholder:'Fabric prompt:\nSubject + motion + speed:\n\nLiquid prompt:\nSubject + motion + speed:\n\nAtmospheric prompt:\nSubject + density + movement:\n\nBest physics render:\nWhy Kling handles it well:',systemPrompt:'You are a Kling AI specialist and physics-driven video director. Review the student\'s 3 physics prompts. Are the motion descriptors specific (slow cascade vs rapid billow)? Are they using the correct physical vocabulary for each material? Give expert prompt adjustments. Max 230 words.'}
};

LESSONS[22]={
  phase:'Phase 3 — Video Ads',
  title:'Day 22: Runway Gen-4.5 — Physics & Director Mode',
  tools:['Runway Gen-4.5'],time:'60 min',tags:['runway','physics','director'],
  videos:[
    {title:'Runway Gen-4.5 Everything New — Physics & Director Mode',channel:'Theoretically Media',duration:'24:50',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=runway+gen+4.5+physics+director+mode+new+features+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e,#16213e)'},
    {title:'Runway vs Kling — Which for Commercial Work?',channel:'AI Advantage',duration:'20:30',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=runway+vs+kling+commercial+work+comparison+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#f953c6,#b91d73)'},
    {title:'Runway Motion Brush Deep Dive',channel:'Matt Wolfe',duration:'18:20',url:'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=runway+motion+brush+deep+dive+tutorial+2026',bg:'linear-gradient(135deg,#667eea,#764ba2)'},
  ],
  inspiration:[
    {name:'Runway ML Explore',desc:'Highest quality Runway outputs. Study the camera movements and physics in professional work.',type:'website',url:'https://runwayml.com/explore',tag:'Reference'},
    {name:'Medium: Controlling Next-Gen Video AI',desc:'The definitive guide to Runway vs Kling vs Veo prompting strategies. Essential reading.',type:'website',url:'https://medium.com/@creativeaininja/how-to-actually-control-next-gen-video-ai-runway-kling-veo-and-sora-prompting-strategies-92ef0055658b',tag:'Deep Dive'},
  ],
  imageRefs:[],
  content:'<div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon purple">🎥</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Runway Gen-4.5 — Think in Forces, Not Visuals</div><div class="concept-card-sub">This is the mental model shift that unlocks Runway\'s true power</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Runway Gen-4.5 solved what was called the "floaty physics" problem. Objects now have <strong>weight, momentum, and mass</strong>. Collisions look real. But you only get this realism if you prompt in the language of forces — not the language of appearances.</p><div class="highlight-box purple"><span class="hb-icon">⚡</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">The Force Language Switch</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>Appearance language (weak):</strong> "A car crashes into a wall"<br><strong>Force language (professional):</strong> "A heavy vintage sedan moving at high velocity impacts a concrete barrier. Momentum carries the front crumple zone forward before the frame decelerates. Glass fragments scatter with trajectory consistent with impact force. Dust cloud displaced by shockwave."<br><br>See the difference? Tell the physics engine HOW things move, not just WHAT moves.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="concept-card"><div class="concept-card-head"><div class="concept-icon blue">🎬</div><div><div class="concept-card-title">Director Mode — Professional Cinematography Control</div><div class="concept-card-sub">Runway recognizes these exact terms — use them precisely</div></div></div><div class="concept-card-body"><p>Runway Gen-4.5\'s Director Mode understands standard cinematography terminology. You can control camera movement independently from subject movement — exactly like a real Director of Photography.</p><div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// RUNWAY DIRECTOR MODE — PRODUCT ORBIT</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this,\'Low angle, wide shot of futuristic sneaker on wet dark asphalt. Camera: smooth arc shot orbiting the shoe clockwise, maintaining the shoe as the central focal point throughout. Subject: shoe remains stationary with perfect surface contact. Lighting: neon reflections shift dynamically across the surface as the camera moves, wet surface reflects ambient city lights. Physics: perfect material consistency throughout rotation. Commercial Nike campaign aesthetic, 10s 16:9.\')">📋 Copy</button></div><div class="prompt-card-body"><span class="prompt-param">Low angle, wide shot of futuristic sneaker on wet dark asphalt.</span><br>Camera: smooth arc shot orbiting the shoe clockwise, maintaining the shoe as the central focal point throughout.<br>Subject: shoe remains stationary with perfect surface contact.<br><span class="prompt-style">Lighting: neon reflections shift dynamically across the surface as the camera moves.</span><br>Physics: perfect material consistency throughout rotation.<br>Commercial Nike campaign aesthetic, 10s 16:9.</div></div><div class="highlight-box green"><span class="hb-icon">💡</span><div class="hb-content"><div class="hb-title">Runway vs Kling — When to Choose Which</div><div class="hb-text"><strong>Choose Runway when:</strong> You need realistic physics impacts, want fine camera control independent of subject, working on car/tech/sports ads, need the Motion Brush for selective movement.<br><strong>Choose Kling when:</strong> You need native audio generation, longer clips (up to 2 min), fabric/liquid/character physics, consistent characters via Elements feature.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class="compare-section"> <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:800;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:10px;">🎬 Appearance Language vs Force Language</div> <div class="compare-toggle-bar"> <button class="compare-tab bad active" id="cmp22-bad" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmp22\',\'bad\')">❌ Appearance (Wrong)</button> <button class="compare-tab good" id="cmp22-good" onclick="switchCompare(\'cmp22\',\'good\')">✅ Force (Right)</button> </div> <div class="compare-panel bad-panel active" id="cmp22-bad-panel"> <div class="compare-prompt">"Beautiful perfume bottle with nice movement and elegant feeling"</div> <div class="compare-annotation"><strong>This is appearance language.</strong> You are describing how it looks, not how it moves. Runway generates video — it needs physical forces, not adjectives. The result: random, weak motion that does not serve the product.</div> </div> <div class="compare-panel good-panel" id="cmp22-good-panel"> <div class="compare-prompt">"Perfume bottle: golden liquid erupts upward from the bottle cap, cascading in slow-motion arc, individual droplets freeze mid-air then reverse, bottle rotates 180° counterclockwise, liquid coats and slides off glass in viscous sheet"</div> <div class="compare-annotation"><strong>This is force language.</strong> Erupts. Cascading. Freeze. Reverse. Rotates. Coats. Slides. Every word describes a physical force or direction. Runway now knows exactly what physics to simulate. Result: cinematic, commercial-grade video.</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card"> <div class="concept-card-head"> <div class="concept-icon blue">💪</div> <div> <div class="concept-card-title">Force Verb Library for Runway</div> <div class="concept-card-sub">Replace every adjective with one of these action words</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card-body"> <p><strong>Liquids:</strong> <span class="vocab-pill">cascades</span> <span class="vocab-pill">erupts upward</span> <span class="vocab-pill">pools slowly</span> <span class="vocab-pill">drips in arc</span> <span class="vocab-pill">viscous pour</span> <span class="vocab-pill">coats the surface</span></p> <p><strong>Fabric:</strong> <span class="vocab-pill">billows outward</span> <span class="vocab-pill">ripples from center</span> <span class="vocab-pill">floats in zero-gravity</span> <span class="vocab-pill">undulates in wave</span> <span class="vocab-pill">collapses in slow motion</span></p> <p><strong>Objects:</strong> <span class="vocab-pill">rotates counterclockwise</span> <span class="vocab-pill">levitates and descends</span> <span class="vocab-pill">shatters into particles</span> <span class="vocab-pill">assembles from fragments</span> <span class="vocab-pill">slides laterally</span></p> <p><strong>Atmosphere:</strong> <span class="vocab-pill">smoke tendrils curl</span> <span class="vocab-pill">steam rises in column</span> <span class="vocab-pill">dust particles drift</span> <span class="vocab-pill">light rays pierce mist</span></p> <div class="prompt-card" style="margin-top:12px;"> <div class="prompt-card-head"><span class="prompt-card-label">// RUNWAY FORCE LANGUAGE — COSMETIC EXAMPLE</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this, \'Luxury face serum dropper: amber serum erupts upward in slow arc from dropper tip, individual suspended droplets catch light and refract into rainbow prisms, droplets reverse course and cascade back into dark glass bottle, bottle rotates 45 degrees as final droplet seals within, camera static close-up with shallow focus on dropper tip\')">📋 Copy</button></div> <div class="prompt-card-body">Serum <span class="prompt-param">erupts upward in slow arc</span>, droplets <span class="prompt-param">refract into rainbow prisms</span>, <span class="prompt-style">reverse and cascade back</span>, bottle rotates 45°</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card"> <div class="concept-card-head"> <div class="concept-icon green">🔧</div> <div> <div class="concept-card-title">Tool Spotlight: Runway Gen-4.5</div> <div class="concept-card-sub">Professional creative control for physics-driven video</div> </div> </div> <div class="concept-card-body"> <p><strong>Runway Gen-4.5</strong> (runwayml.com) — Motion Brushes paint where movement happens. Act One captures facial performance. Director Mode controls camera independently. Paid ($12/month). <a href="https://runwayml.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:700;">Open Runway →</a></p> <p><em>This lesson: force language — Runway needs physical verbs (erupts, cascades, rotates) not adjectives.</em></p> </div> </div>',
  assignment:{title:'Day 22: Runway Force Language — Product Physics',emoji:'🎥',desc:'Write a Runway Gen-4.5 prompt using force language (not appearance language) for a product that benefits from physics — cosmetics, food, or fashion.',deliverables:['Product chosen and why Runway suits it','Your Runway prompt using force language (not \'beautiful\' — but \'cascading,\' \'erupting,\' \'rippling\')','What physical forces did you describe — and what emotion do they create?','How would you combine this with a Midjourney still image as input?'],placeholder:'Product:\nWhy Runway suits it:\n\nForce language prompt:\nForces described:\nEmotion created:\n\nMidjourney → Runway workflow plan:',systemPrompt:'You are a Runway Gen-4.5 specialist. Review the student\'s force language prompt. Are they truly using motion/force vocabulary (not appearance words)? Does the physical language match the product category? Give them 2 stronger force verbs they should try. Max 220 words.'}
};

